.TH GRAFANA-UTIL-DASHBOARD-IMPORT 1 "2026-04-03" "grafana-util 0.14.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
grafana\-util\-dashboard\-import \- Import classic dashboard JSON or native dashboard schema v2 resource JSON through the matching Grafana API.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B grafana-util dashboard import [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import classic dashboard JSON or native dashboard schema v2 resource JSON through the matching Grafana API.
.PP
Use this when you have a local export tree for dashboards that are owned by Grafana's API state and need to push dashboards back into Grafana, either live or as a dry run. The default \-\-input\-format auto detects the export lane and selects the matching API. Classic import consumes raw/ or provisioning/ inputs; native schema v2 import consumes resource\-v2/ JSON resources when the exact v2 collection endpoint is served. The command does not consume the Grafana UI prompt/ lane.
.SH BEFORE / AFTER
.IP \(bu 2
Before: import is a blind replay step, and you find folder, org, or schema problems only after the live call.
.IP \(bu 2
After: import becomes a controlled replay step that can be previewed first with \-\-dry\-run, then executed with clearer intent.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-input\-dir
source directory for a classic lane, an exported resource\-v2/ directory, or a combined export root.
.TP
.B \-\-input\-format
defaults to auto; choose raw, provisioning, or the explicit native resource lane resource\-v2 to bypass detection.
.TP
.B \-\-resource\-namespace
authoritative App Platform destination namespace for resource\-v2 import. Auto mode infers a single source namespace and uses default only when source documents omit it; pass this flag to override the inferred value. Explicit \-\-input\-format resource\-v2 uses default when the flag is omitted.
.TP
.B \-\-local, \-\-run, \-\-run\-id
read the source dashboard lane from the artifact workspace instead of passing \-\-input\-dir.
.TP
.B \-\-org\-id, \-\-use\-export\-org, \-\-only\-org\-id, \-\-create\-missing\-orgs
control cross\-org routing.
.TP
.B \-\-import\-folder\-uid
force a destination folder UID.
.TP
.B \-\-ensure\-folders, \-\-replace\-existing, \-\-update\-existing\-only
control import behavior.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-matching\-folder\-path, \-\-require\-matching\-export\-org, \-\-strict\-schema, \-\-target\-schema\-version
safety checks.
.TP
.B \-\-import\-message
revision message stored in Grafana.
.TP
.B \-\-interactive, \-\-dry\-run, \-\-table, \-\-json, \-\-output\-format, \-\-output\-columns, \-\-list\-columns, \-\-no\-header, \-\-progress, \-\-verbose
preview and reporting controls. Use \-\-output\-columns all for the full dry\-run table.
.SH SUCCESS CRITERIA
.IP \(bu 2
dry\-run shows the expected create/update actions before you touch the live server
.IP \(bu 2
dry\-run also surfaces live dashboard target evidence when Grafana already owns the UID, including provisioned or managed\-state warnings
.IP \(bu 2
the destination org and folder routing are explicit enough to review
.IP \(bu 2
the selected input lane matches the replay goal: raw, provisioning, or resource\-v2, not prompt; auto mode reports its choice on stderr
.IP \(bu 2
Git Sync or file\-provisioned targets are treated as source\-owned and routed back to their repository or provisioning workflow
.SH FAILURE CHECKS
.IP \(bu 2
if folder or org placement looks wrong, verify the routing flags before re\-running live import
.IP \(bu 2
if the replay looks too destructive, stop at \-\-dry\-run and inspect the export tree first
.IP \(bu 2
if Grafana reports a provisioned or Git Sync\-managed dashboard at the target UID, do not retry with a direct import; update the owning source and redeploy through that lane
.IP \(bu 2
if the schema check blocks replay, confirm whether the source tree needs normalization before import
.IP \(bu 2
if resource\-v2 reports that the API is unavailable, verify Grafana serves the v2 /apis endpoint; do not retry the same resource through classic import
.IP \(bu 2
if resource\-v2 selects the wrong namespace, pass \-\-resource\-namespace explicitly and review the dry\-run; source metadata.namespace is not authoritative
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Import classic dashboard JSON or native dashboard schema v2 resource JSON through the matching Grafana API.
.EX
grafana-util dashboard import --url http://localhost:3000 --basic-user admin --basic-password admin --input-dir ./dashboards/raw --replace-existing
.EE
